# Trained weight files are written by every run INCLUDING smoke tests, so
# they are not tracked by default — an 8-genome, 1-generation smoke result
# sitting in the repo looks exactly like a real one, and the whole point of
# weights.js refusing an uncommented non-zero is that a number has to carry
# the run that earned it.
#
# A result worth keeping gets committed deliberately, with its provenance
# in the commit message: git add -f trained.<mode>.json
trained.*.json
